# Project-local Adder startup.
# Keep the REPL quiet: no "In [n]:" input prompt and no "Out[n]:" result label.
# The continuation prompt is EMPTY on purpose. Adder's indentation is
# significant, so a prompt made of spaces is actively harmful: those columns
# are undeletable, so backspacing to column 0 still LOOKS indented, and a
# correctly-aligned `else:` renders as if it were nested one level in.
# With "" the indentation on screen is the indentation in the buffer.
setf *prompt-in* (fn (n) "")
setf *prompt-out* (fn (n) "")
setf *prompt-cont* (fn (n) "")
